{%- comment -%}
  The figures of one CV entry, from the hand-kept _data/cv_figures.yml (keyed by entry id); nothing is drawn when there are none.
  Parameter: entry. Markup: <div class="cv-figures"> of <figure class="cv-figure"> (an <img> and a <figcaption>). The image carries
  data-zoomable, which the theme's zoom script (al_img_tools, loaded on every page while enable_medium_zoom is true in _config.yml)
  selects to enlarge it on click. src goes through relative_url; alt and caption are plain text and escaped. The thumbnail box is
  sized in CSS (_sass/_cv.scss) because the files' dimensions are not known here. Lazy loading keeps a closed <details> from
  fetching its images.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign figures = site.data.cv_figures[include.entry.id] -%}
{%- if figures.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="cv-figures">
    {%- for figure in figures -%}
      <figure class="cv-figure">
        <img src="{{ figure.src | relative_url }}" alt="{{ figure.alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-zoomable>
        <figcaption>{{ figure.caption | escape }}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
